    "date": "2026-03-17T11:25:25",
    "comment": "Nupe-Nupe-Tako (nup-nup) = 3 (Wider communication). De facto language of provincial identity in Niger, Kwara, and Koji states; possibly in Abuja Capital Territory, widespread. Became the LWC in Central Nigeria in the early 19th century. Used in trade, animal husbandry, agriculture, oral literature, music, and religion."
